Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:33:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] maki: warm reset (keep RRAM, counters, flash), and bootrom
 --reboot

emu_warm_reset restarts the CPU at boot0 and rebuilds the volatile device fabric and RAM, but
keeps what a real chip keeps across a power cycle: the RRAM array, the one-way counters, the IFR
fuse block, and the external SPI flash (swap + PDDB). bootrom --reboot uses it to boot again.

This exercises the two-boot part of the trust chain: boot0 writes the boot1 key manifest into
the receipt slots on the first boot and compares against them on the next. Verified with the
factory stages: "Boot1 receipts OK" on both the cold and the warm boot, "Collateral erased"
both times (the factory boot1 manifest carries Baochip keys).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
